<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

!! Contract

``<<~ papalohe from=`lar:///a.b.c/x` to=`lar:///a.b.c/y`>>`` declares a reaction-family edge — an event wire running from a source event to a target function. The compile layer reads the annotation and wires the reaction-graph edge.

The argument RUN carries the whole assertion: `#slot FROM -> TO listenable:EventName subscribable:Name`. The `#slot` fragment names the wire so a `kukali` wait in the same carrier can name it back through `trigger`.

''The widget reads the run, not the slots.'' A from, an arrow and a to compose ONE assertion, so splitting them across positional slots would let the shape be got subtly wrong; `args` hands the definition the text as written.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/render`>>

!! Render

''The page stays clear.'' A wire governs execution and never layout, so the widget renders a hidden annotation:

```
<span class="lar-papalohe" data-papalohe-args=<<args>> hidden="true"/>
```

The declaration rides in `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/sigil-papalohe.tid` with `lar-kind: edge-sugar` and the match pattern that captures fragment, from, to, `listenable` and `subscribable`.

<<~/ahu>>

